Date: Thu, 10 Sep 2026 11:49:25 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 2/3] fix(stack): show a plain notice and one full reference
 per line

The component panel restated the inside of each package as a list of modules,
each with its charts written as a name, a version and a repository, and its
images as references. Which module something belongs to is structure, not
identity, and the package definition carries it authoritatively at the pinned
commit.

So the module scaffolding goes and every line is one full reference:

    quay.io/okdp/charts/polaris-admin:1.0.0
    polaris:1.3.0-incubating (https://downloads.apache.org/incubator/polaris/helm-chart/)
    docker.io/apache/polaris:1.3.0-incubating
    quay.io/okdp/polaris-console:v0.1.1

Anything published to a registry is complete on its own. A chart served from a
Helm repository is not, so its repository follows it: the reference and its
website, nothing more. Local charts are vendored in the package repo and have no
reference, so they stay out. Flattening also collapses duplicates the module
boundaries preserved: Polaris used polaris-admin in two modules and listed it
twice. 69 entries render, 67 distinct.

The heading follows the content: "Included modules" becomes "Included
references", and the key moves from details.modules to details.references.

Ingress NGINX's retired-upstream notice renders here too, as plain text with no
badge or label. d71d554 removed the pre-release badge from the summary row and
nothing puts one back; the sentence carries the meaning on its own.

That commit's leftovers go as well: ComponentRow still computed an isPrerelease
nothing read, and badges.prerelease sat in both locale files with no consumer.

